# MongoDB

Enforcement: **B**.

## Distinctives

- Embed vs reference based on access patterns and document size limits.
- Multi-document transactions exist but have costs — prefer single-document atomicity when possible.
- Indexes required for production query filters; unused indexes still cost writes.
- Schema validation can help but is not a full relational constraint system.
- Change streams / oplog consumers need idempotency.

## Do not

- Assume joins are free
- Grow unbounded arrays in documents
- Skip schema evolution planning for existing collections
